<section class="hero py-56-64 om-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="hero-title-clamp">The Caregiver Sanctuary Model</h1>
    <p class="lede om-hero-sub">Caregiver Wellness, Rooted in Community</p>
    <p class="om-hero-text">Family caregivers do so much, often without the support they need for themselves.</p>
    <p class="om-hero-text">At Legacy, we believe caregiver support should be easier to find, easier to access, and available beyond a single appointment, event, or conversation.</p>
    <p class="om-hero-text">The Caregiver Sanctuary Model brings together the services we provide and the relationships we’ve built throughout the community. It’s how we help caregivers find relief, build confidence, connect with others, and make room for their own well-being.</p>
    <p class="om-hero-text">Our work is especially focused on families caring for someone living with dementia, while recognizing that many caregiving experiences share similar challenges.</p>
    <p class="om-hero-close"><strong>We use the power of community to care for the caregiver.</strong></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="om-section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="omHowTitle">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="om-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">How Our Model Works</span>
      <h2 id="omHowTitle">Different Needs. One Connected Approach.</h2>
      <p>No two caregivers have the same experience. What helps one person may not be what another needs.</p>
      <p>Instead of expecting caregivers to figure everything out on their own, we work with them to understand what’s happening in their lives and connect them with the right support.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="om-model" role="list" aria-label="The Caregiver Sanctuary Model: five areas around the family caregiver">
      <div class="om-center" aria-hidden="true"><span class="om-center-icon"><svg class="om-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.6-7 10-7 10z"/></svg></span><strong>Family Caregiver</strong></div>
      <div class="om-area om-area-1" role="listitem">
        <span class="om-icon-wrap"><svg class="om-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M20 14.5A8 8 0 1 1 9.5 4a6.5 6.5 0 0 0 10.5 10.5z"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Respite &amp; Relief</h3>
        <p>Everyone needs a break. Through our respite services and community connections, we help caregivers find opportunities to step away, recharge, and take care of other parts of their lives.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="om-area om-area-2" role="listitem">
        <span class="om-icon-wrap"><svg class="om-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 5.5c3-1 6-1 9 1 3-2 6-2 9-1V19c-3-1-6-1-9 1-3-2-6-2-9-1z"/><path d="M12 6.5V20"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Education &amp; Guidance</h3>
        <p>Caregiving comes with questions, decisions, and situations people aren’t always prepared for. We offer practical education, helpful resources, and guidance to make those challenges a little easier to navigate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="om-area om-area-3" role="listitem">
        <span class="om-icon-wrap"><svg class="om-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="3"/><circle cx="16.5" cy="9.5" r="2.5"/><path d="M2.5 20c0-3.3 2.5-6 5.5-6s5.5 2.7 5.5 6"/><path d="M14 14.6c.8-.4 1.6-.6 2.5-.6 2.8 0 5 2.4 5 5.5"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Connection &amp; Peer Support</h3>
        <p>There’s something powerful about talking with someone who understands. Our support groups and caregiver gatherings create space to share experiences, ask questions, and feel less alone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="om-area om-area-4" role="listitem">
        <span class="om-icon-wrap"><svg class="om-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 21c-4.4 0-7-3.4-7-7.5S8 6 12 8c4-2 7 1.4 7 5.5S16.4 21 12 21z"/><path d="M12 8c0-2 1-3.5 3-4.5"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Wellness &amp; Restoration</h3>
        <p>Caregivers have needs of their own. We create opportunities for rest, creativity, social connection, and activities that allow caregivers to focus on themselves for a change.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="om-area om-area-5" role="listitem">
        <span class="om-icon-wrap"><svg class="om-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 21V10l9-6 9 6v11"/><path d="M9 21v-6h6v6"/></svg></span>
        <h3>Community Partnerships</h3>
        <p>We work with churches, healthcare providers, businesses, wellness organizations, and other community partners to bring more resources and opportunities within reach.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="om-note">These aren’t separate pieces of our work. Together, they shape how we care for caregivers.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="om-section om-tint" id="journey" aria-labelledby="omJourneyTitle">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="om-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Caregiver Journey</span>
      <h2 id="omJourneyTitle">Meeting Caregivers Where They Are</h2>
      <p>Some caregivers come to us looking for respite. Others need information, emotional support, or help figuring out where to start.</p>
      <p>Whatever brings them to Legacy, our goal is to make sure they feel heard and know what options are available.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="om-timeline">
      <li class="om-step"><span class="om-step-num">01</span><div><h3>Connect</h3><p>Caregivers find Legacy through referrals, community events, healthcare providers, partner organizations, or by reaching out directly.</p></div></li>
      <li class="om-step"><span class="om-step-num">02</span><div><h3>Listen</h3><p>We take time to understand their experiences, concerns, and what kind of help would make a difference.</p></div></li>
      <li class="om-step"><span class="om-step-num">03</span><div><h3>Support</h3><p>Together, we identify services and resources that fit their needs, whether that’s respite, education, wellness, or connecting with other caregivers.</p></div></li>
      <li class="om-step"><span class="om-step-num">04</span><div><h3>Stay Connected</h3><p>Needs change. We make room for continued conversations, check-ins, and opportunities to connect as caregiving circumstances evolve.</p></div></li>
      <li class="om-step"><span class="om-step-num">05</span><div><h3>Learn &amp; Improve</h3><p>We pay attention to what caregivers tell us, what they’re using, and where barriers still exist. That helps us make our services better.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="om-section" id="community" aria-labelledby="omCommunityTitle">
  <div class="container om-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Why Community Matters</span>
      <h2 id="omCommunityTitle">Caregiving Happens Beyond the Healthcare Setting</h2>
    <p>A doctor’s appointment might last 20 minutes. Caregiving continues long after that appointment ends.</p>
    <p>Families are managing medications, appointments, changing behaviors, household responsibilities, and the emotional weight that can come with caring for someone they love.</p>
    <p>Healthcare providers play an important role, but they can’t always address everything happening in a caregiver’s daily life.</p>
    <p class="om-emphasis"><strong>That’s why community matters.</strong></p>
    <p>Legacy works to connect caregivers with people, services, and opportunities that support them outside of traditional healthcare settings.</p>
    <p>We’re not trying to replace the work healthcare providers or other organizations do. We want to help connect the pieces so caregivers aren’t left figuring everything out alone.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="om-section om-tint" id="partnerships" aria-labelledby="omPartnersTitle">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="om-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Partnerships That Make a Difference</span>
      <h2 id="omPartnersTitle">Supporting Caregivers Is Something We Can Do Together</h2>
      <p>No single organization can meet every caregiver’s needs. We believe stronger relationships between healthcare, workplaces, and community organizations can make support easier to access.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="om-partners">
      <div class="card om-partner"><h3>Healthcare Partnerships</h3><p>Working with healthcare organizations to connect family caregivers with education, wellness opportunities, respite resources, and support beyond medical appointments.</p></div>
      <div class="card om-partner"><h3>Workplace Partnerships</h3><p>Helping employers explore ways to support employees who are balancing work with caring for a family member.</p></div>
      <div class="card om-partner"><h3>Community &amp; Faith Partnerships</h3><p>Working with churches, local businesses, wellness providers, and community organizations to create more places and opportunities for caregivers to find support.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="om-note">We’re continuing to build relationships with organizations that share our commitment to caregiver well-being.</p>
    <p class="text-center mt-24"><a href="get-involved.html#partner" class="btn btn-coral">Explore Partnership Opportunities</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="om-section" id="learning" aria-labelledby="omLearningTitle">
  <div class="container om-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">Learning From Experience</span>
      <h2 id="omLearningTitle">What We’ve Learned Is Shaping What’s Next</h2>
    <p>Legacy didn’t start with a fully developed model. We’ve spent years working directly with caregivers, trying different approaches, listening, and learning along the way.</p>
    <p>We’ve seen the value of respite, the connections that happen in support groups, and how much it matters when caregivers have an opportunity to focus on themselves.</p>
    <p>We’ve also learned that offering something doesn’t always mean caregivers can access it. Timing, responsibilities, transportation, and other barriers can affect participation.</p>
    <p>Those experiences are helping us think differently about how we deliver support.</p>
    <p>As we move forward, we’re putting more intention into how we collect data, gather feedback, and understand the difference our services make.</p>
    <p>We want to know what’s working, what caregivers still need, and how we can make this model stronger.</p>
    <p class="om-emphasis"><em><strong>Our goal isn’t simply to reach more caregivers. It’s to make sure the support we’re providing is meaningful, accessible, and sustainable.</strong></em></p>
  </div>
</section>

